course: dictionary
lesson: 13902
title: An old name and a better one
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words were once normal but are now old-fashioned, and some can hurt people. «Lapp» is one of these. It is an old name for the Sámi, the Indigenous people of the far north of Norway, Sweden, Finland and Russia.
explain: Many Sámi find «Lapp» offensive, which means it can hurt or insult them. So today we say «Sámi». Context can show you this: «Old books call them Lapps, but most Sámi prefer their own name.» The word «but» shows the two names are not treated the same.
explain: Read the clues around a word. Here they tell you that «Lapp» is old and that the people themselves choose «Sámi». When you write about a people, use the name they use for themselves.
fact: «Lapp» is an old name for the Sámi people.
fact: Many Sámi find the word «Lapp» offensive, so it is best to avoid it.
fact: The Sámi live in the far north of Norway, Sweden, Finland and Russia, in a region called Lapland.
fact: The Sámi herd reindeer and have their own languages and parliaments.
exercise: «Old books call the Sámi Lapps, but many Sámi find that name offensive.» What name should you use today? | Lapland | Lapp | *Sámi | Norsemen
exercise: «Lapp» is an old name for which people? | *The Sámi, the Indigenous people of the far north | Reindeer farmers from Spain | People who live in cities in the south | The Vikings of Norway
exercise: Which word should replace «Lapps» in a modern text about reindeer herders in the Arctic? | Norse | Vikings | *Sámi | Lapps
test: Why might a writer avoid the word «Lapp» today? | *Many Sámi find it offensive | It is only used in one small town | It means happy and friendly | It is too short to be clear
test: What is the Arctic region called where the Sámi live? | *Lapland | Lappland Park | Norway Hills | Sámi Sea
exam: Which word is the respectful name the Sámi use for their own people? | Laplander | Lapps | *Sámi | Lapp
